   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u002",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "Who is it—oh... Queen Vasantha Devi?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d001",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 69,
       "printed_page": 68
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u003",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வசந்",
    "text": "Are Swami's thoughts on God?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d002",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 69,
       "printed_page": 68
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "This sets up the `ஆண்டவன் / ஆண்டு கொண்டிருப்பவன்` wordplay in Ugrasenan's reply."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u004",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "Not about the Lord. About the one who is ruling... sit down, my delight.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d003",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The Lord/ruler turn in `ஆண்டவன் / ஆண்டு கொண்டிருப்பவன்` is retained rather than flattened."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u005",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வ. சே.",
    "text": "Have some fruit juice.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d004",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u006",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "First I shall drink the nectar of your gaze, my dear!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d005",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The source's `பார்வை ரசம்` image is preserved as gaze-nectar rather than reduced to ordinary flirtation."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u007",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "சேனா",
    "text": "How many days it has been since I saw you.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d006",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u008",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "தோழி",
    "text": "Did you call me, Amma?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d007",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u009",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "சேனா",
    "text": "No, go away.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d008",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u010",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "(Running his hand through her hair) Ah! A gathering of clouds. (Showing her teeth) A jasmine garden. (Stroking her cheek) A field of roses!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d009",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The cloud / jasmine-garden / rose-field sequence and its source-attached gestures are retained in order."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u011",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "சேனா",
    "text": "Swami!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d010",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u012",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "Altogether, the very limit of delight!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d011",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u013",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "சேனா",
    "text": "Yes... how have you planned all the plans?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d012",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful",
     "notes": [
      "The source's repetition of `திட்டங்கள் / திட்டியிருக்கிறீர்கள்` remains audible."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u014",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "Splendidly! All the important parts of the palace are being occupied by our warriors disguised as mendicants. One command from us is enough—war! Purushothaman under arrest!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d013",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The abrupt `போர்! புருஷோத்தமன் கைது!` military cadence is preserved."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u015",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "சேனா",
    "text": "Even war will not be necessary. I have Purushothaman's soldiers in the palm of my hand.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d014",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "`என் கைக்குள் போட்டு வைத்திருக்கிறேன்` remains a control-in-the-hand image rather than being generalized."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u016",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "Sabash! What if war does come? Once enemy troops have entered the palace, who can resist and win?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d015",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u017",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "சேனா",
    "text": "Have the enemy troops come only into the palace?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d016",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The line deliberately opens the sexual double meaning that follows."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u018",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "உக்",
    "text": "You mean they have come all the way into the inner chambers? This is not to fight. To surrender.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d017",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The palace/inner-chambers and fight/surrender double entendre is preserved without explanatory expansion."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s044-u019",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "சேனா",
    "text": "I will come tonight.",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-044.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-044.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s044-d018",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 70,
       "printed_page": 69
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "semantic-poetic",
     "notes": [
      "The concise closing line is left to carry its source double meaning without added explanation."
     ]
    }
   }
  ]
 }
